codex
Built the Track B generator around the paper’s native Problem 4 pseudo-key task and Theorem 22’s factoring connection. [The paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/0803.0845) defines the exact remainder and superincreasing conditions in Sections 4.1–4.2.

Deliverables:

- [gen_0803_0845.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0803.0845/gen_0803_0845.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0803.0845/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0803.0845/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0803.0845/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0803.0845/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0803.0845/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Results:

- All nine local gates pass.
- Guessing: 0/200,000; exact density `2^-103`.
- Five attacks: 0/8 each.
- Reference GCD: 8/8, averaging 481 Euclidean divisions.
- Compact finite-difference route: 23 operations.
- Worst answer: 61 characters, 16 estimated tokens, 2 atoms.
- Canonical-key tests: 60/60 invariant; 20/20 unrelated instances distinct.

The result is not submission-ready because every OpenRouter call returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” Consequently, bare/hinted/placebo each have 0 valid attempts, and no hardness verdict is claimed. The harness-authored error records are preserved. Once quota is available, rerun:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/0803.0845
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_0803_0845.py
```

No `REJECTED.md` was created. I also removed the incidental artifact and “done” claim created by a failed dry submission; both are reproducible.
